  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Let $a=t\\,i+4j-k$ and $b=2i-j.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $t.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular.\n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na\u22a5b\\,\u27f9\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =t\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2t-4+0 \\\\  & =2t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2t-4 & =0 \\\\ 2t & =4 \\\\ t & =2 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
